---

Checkpoint types

- "best.pt" = the checkpoint with the best validation result. Lower validation loss is better.
- "live.pt" = latest checkpoint used to continue/resume training.
- "base.pt" = starting checkpoint of the training run.
- "history/" = old checkpoint versions kept as backups when "best.pt" or "live.pt" is replaced.

During training:

base.pt  → saved at the start
live.pt  → updated during training
best.pt  → updated only when validation improves
history/ → keeps replaced/older checkpoints

Do not manually replace "best.pt" with a worse checkpoint.

_TRAIN

python scripts\generate_facts.py --repeats 20
python scripts\train.py --config configs\char_transformer.yaml --set run_name=ored_v2 --set training.epochs=40 --set training.device=cuda

---

If you want to start from another checkpoint

python scripts\train.py --config configs\char_transformer.yaml --set run_name=ored_v2 --init-from checkpoints\char_transformer_v2\best.pt --set training.epochs=40 --set training.device=cuda

"--init-from" means start a new run using the other checkpoint's weights.

If training was stopped and you want to continue it

python scripts\train.py --config configs\char_transformer.yaml --resume-live --set training.epochs=40

"--resume-live" means continue from the saved "live.pt" training state.

---

Save checkpoints manually if needed

Put a checkpoint into history:

python scripts\checkpoints.py save FILE.pt --as history --config configs\char_transformer.yaml

Put a checkpoint into best:

python scripts\checkpoints.py save FILE.pt --as best --config configs\char_transformer.yaml

Put a checkpoint into live:

python scripts\checkpoints.py save FILE.pt --as live --config configs\char_transformer.yaml

- "best" only replaces "best.pt" if it scores better on validation.
- "best --force" can replace it manually if absolutely needed.
- "live" must contain everything required to continue training.
- Replaced "best.pt" or "live.pt" is kept in "history/".

---

Merge online-learning result into best

After an online-learning session creates a live checkpoint:

_RUN

python scripts\checkpoints.py merge-live --config configs\char_transformer.yaml

---

This compares the online-learning "live.pt" with the current "best.pt" on the same validation data.

If live is better:

live.pt → best.pt
old best.pt → history/

If live is not better:

best.pt stays unchanged

Example:

live = 3.07018
best = 3.37613

Since lower validation loss is better, the live checkpoint becomes "best.pt".

